## Why This Is Asked
Tests mapping of high-level operations to a classic data-structure primitive (Fenwick tree) with dynamic growth.

## Key Concepts
- Fenwick tree (Binary Indexed Tree)
- 1-based indexing
- dynamic growth and delta updates
- handling duplicates in values

## Code Example
```javascript
class Fenwick {
  constructor(n){ this.n=n; this.ft=new Array(n+1).fill(0); this.arr=[] }
  append(v){ this.arr.push(v); const i=this.arr.length; this.add(i,v); }
  add(i,delta){ for(; i<=this.n; i+=i&-i) this.ft[i]+=delta; }
  update(i,v){ const delta=v-this.arr[i-1]; this.arr[i-1]=v; this.add(i,delta); }
  sum(i){ let s=0; for(; i>0; i-=i&-i) s+=this.ft[i]; return s; }
  range(l,r){ return this.sum(r)-this.sum(l-1); }
}
```

